        "department": null,
        "description": "Inclusive Design is a methodology that enables and draws on the full range of human diversity i.e. including and learning from people with a range of perspectives. The objective of this project-based course is to learn about the background, principles and purpose of inclusive design, accessibility and universal design. The students will learn the process of inclusive design, how to think in an 'inclusive' way and apply that knowledge to a group project. Assistive technologies and multi-sensory interaction technologies are primarily aimed at including braoder range of users and these kind of solutions are needed for creating more accessible environment and experiences. By the end of the course, the students will be able to critique the accessibility of existing design solutions and be able to improve them by considering these features. They will also be able to include more users and different user perspectives in their design thinking process.",
